## Hypothesis

Given the defect (a) is invisible in wide uniform fills but visible in fine/thin content, (b) is tied to the display's physical horizontal center column (x = width/2 = 360 for this 720px-wide panel) rather than to any particular widget's own bounding-box center, and (c) persists across LVGL software rasterizer thread count, DMA2D usage, and buffering mode changes, we suspect the root cause lies in LVGL's own software draw/blend code path (`lv_draw_sw_blend_to_rgb565` or the buffer/stride handling around it) rather than in the ESP-IDF MIPI-DSI/DPI driver or the `esp_lvgl_adapter` copy/flush logic — though this has not been conclusively isolated given the caveat above, and we would appreciate guidance on how to test this more rigorously (e.g. a way to log/inspect the actual rendered buffer content at specific columns before it is sent to the panel, rather than relying on photography).

## Reproduction (minimal)

